# Line endings are pinned to LF for everything textual.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows but *built and run* on Linux (WSL and
# GitHub's runners). Git's default `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows would check
# these files out with CRLF, and a CRLF shebang does not fail as "wrong line
# ending" — it fails as `bash: scripts/app-build.sh: /usr/bin/env: bad
# interpreter` or a bare "No such file or directory", which points at the script
# instead of at the cause. Pinning it here means the checkout matches on every
# machine without anyone having to configure Git.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never line-ending converted, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.so binary
*.jks binary
*.keystore binary
*.zip binary
